If somebody respect his own religion or his
own identity, that somebody should respect

00:19:46.659 --> 00:19:49.320
to the identity and religion of the other
one.

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:51.750
This empathy is important.

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:55.370
But freedom of speech, that does not mean
freedom of insult.

00:19:55.370 --> 00:19:58.600
Here we are in a very civilized atmosphere.

00:19:58.600 --> 00:20:03.070
I am talking and anybody can criticize me.

00:20:03.070 --> 00:20:04.110
Anybody can say anything to me.

00:20:04.110 --> 00:20:05.640
HAASS: We'll get to that part later.

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:06.710
DAVUTOGLU: Yes.

00:20:06.710 --> 00:20:07.710
I know.

00:20:07.710 --> 00:20:08.710
I know.

00:20:08.710 --> 00:20:11.070
That's what I am inviting them to criticize.

00:20:11.070 --> 00:20:17.720
But if somebody insults, it is against the
cultural civilized life.

00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:21.340
Or I can defend myself or my position.

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:27.440
But if I, looking at someone, assume that
he's from a particular religion, and looking

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:34.370
at him or her, insulting that religion is
not only insulting the religion but insulting

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:35.680
that personality.

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:39.289
HAASS: Who decides that in a democratic society?

00:20:39.289 --> 00:20:42.580
DAVUTOGLU: The social values will decide.

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:43.669
That's more important.

00:20:43.669 --> 00:20:52.140
It might be in some social atmosphere, some
words might not be as insulting as others.

00:20:52.140 --> 00:21:02.240
But the belief and certain values are part
of the identity of every individual.

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:08.779
And respect to the dignity of individual is
a civilized value as well like freedom of

00:21:08.779 --> 00:21:10.250
speech.

00:21:10.250 --> 00:21:19.250
If somebody insults Prophet Muhammad or Jesus
in my�in our presence, it is not only insulting

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:20.250
that.

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:21.250
Why?

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:22.860
Why do we use insult?

00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:26.850
Language�language of hatred should not be
used.

00:21:26.850 --> 00:21:34.250
In a civilized democratic society there should
be any criticism, but not insult.

00:21:34.250 --> 00:21:36.009
This is the main difference.

00:21:36.009 --> 00:21:45.010
For us, Turkey, for our society, for centuries
we lived in a multi-cultural, multi-religious

00:21:45.010 --> 00:21:46.010
society.

00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:50.460
Jews, Muslims, Christians lived in the same
street next to each other in Istanbul.

00:21:50.460 --> 00:21:57.289
I know you came several times and I am very
happy to hear that you also visited 10 days.

00:21:57.289 --> 00:22:03.600
When you go to certain streets, mosque, synagogue
and church are wall-to-wall.

00:22:03.600 --> 00:22:09.460
And meaning that those who are going to mosque,
they greet Christians and Jews, and those

00:22:09.460 --> 00:22:12.179
who are going to synagogues they greet others.

00:22:12.179 --> 00:22:21.860
There, in such an atmosphere, there will be
no culture of violence and culture of insult.

00:22:21.860 --> 00:22:27.259
If there is violence to the certain societies,
it is because of the absence of a tradition

00:22:27.259 --> 00:22:28.429
of multiculturalism.

00:22:28.429 --> 00:22:34.100
And if there is an insult culture, again,
that is the absence.

00:22:34.100 --> 00:22:38.039
I was in Paris defending freedom of speech.

00:22:38.039 --> 00:22:48.130
But next day I went to a mosque in Berlin
which was burned by racists in Europe.

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:49.840
These are not contradictory.

00:22:49.840 --> 00:22:57.190
We have to respect dignities, dignity of our
counterparts.

00:22:57.190 --> 00:23:02.360
But at the same time we have to give full
right of freedom of criticism, not freedom

00:23:02.360 --> 00:23:03.990
of insult.

00:23:03.990 --> 00:23:09.570
HAASS: Also on the domestic side, the so-called
domestic security package.

00:23:09.570 --> 00:23:11.690
Why is something like that necessary?

00:23:11.690 --> 00:23:17.529
Why is there so much concern about placing
a ceiling or limiting the right of assembly

00:23:17.529 --> 00:23:20.320
and the right of protest?

00:23:20.320 --> 00:23:21.799
What are�what's the consideration?

00:23:21.799 --> 00:23:27.820
DAVUTOGLU: I wish to give the English translation
to you and all the audience here about this

00:23:27.820 --> 00:23:28.820
law.

00:23:28.820 --> 00:23:30.770
What is the substance of it?

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:33.409
It is not just security.

00:23:33.409 --> 00:23:38.899
It is security and protecting liberties law.

00:23:38.899 --> 00:23:40.740
Why?

00:23:40.740 --> 00:23:48.999
Because in last year, 6 and 7 October, after
we established the government, there were

00:23:48.999 --> 00:23:58.350
several violent terrorist attacks in cities,
especially in Southeastern Anatolia by certain

00:23:58.350 --> 00:23:59.379
terrorist groups.

00:23:59.379 --> 00:24:08.760
They used Molotov cocktails to burn houses,
and some young people being killed, and doing

00:24:08.760 --> 00:24:09.760
demonstrations.

00:24:09.760 --> 00:24:13.470
They used certain methods as if they are demonstrating.

00:24:13.470 --> 00:24:16.580
They are not peaceful demonstrations.

00:24:16.580 --> 00:24:26.169
And based on all these very alarming experiences,
provocated by some circles like creating an

00:24:26.169 --> 00:24:29.090
atmosphere like in Syria or Iraq.

00:24:29.090 --> 00:24:33.220
We decided to take certain measures.

00:24:33.220 --> 00:24:37.629
But these measures, the basic criteria that
was 7th of October.

00:24:37.629 --> 00:24:43.669
15th of October I got everything from Ministry
of Domestic Affairs.

00:24:43.669 --> 00:24:46.610
And the basic criteria is EU standards.

00:24:46.610 --> 00:24:51.830
In this package there is nothing contradictory
to EU standards.

00:24:51.830 --> 00:24:59.389
Therefore, for example Molotov cocktails,
you know it is prohibited everywhere in Europe,

00:24:59.389 --> 00:25:00.850
everywhere in United States.

00:25:00.850 --> 00:25:08.389
And in certain states here in U.S. there is
a very high penalty for this, $2 million penalty

00:25:08.389 --> 00:25:10.899
and four years penalty.

00:25:10.899 --> 00:25:21.299
In Britain three PKK supporters, because of
using the Molotov cocktail was judged�charged

00:25:21.299 --> 00:25:24.220
for fourteen years.

00:25:24.220 --> 00:25:29.830
In Turkish case, in our case, there was no
direct reference to Molotov cocktail.

00:25:29.830 --> 00:25:38.289
And therefore, these people, not doing demonstration,
doing violent action, were using Molotov cocktails.

00:25:38.289 --> 00:25:42.019
And several young ladies were burned in the
past.

00:25:42.019 --> 00:25:50.100
What we are doing in this is we are prohibiting
Molotov cocktails to be used in demonstrations.

00:25:50.100 --> 00:25:58.049
And in order to secure free demonstrations
we said that nobody could cover the face.

00:25:58.049 --> 00:26:02.029
They're covering the face and attacking the
other side.

00:26:02.029 --> 00:26:06.549
There were several clashes in demonstrations,
so-called demonstrations.

00:26:06.549 --> 00:26:09.210
And this is according to E.U.

00:26:09.210 --> 00:26:10.340
standards.

00:26:10.340 --> 00:26:24.399
The most discussed item was the police and
the legal�how many hours you can keep someone.

00:26:24.399 --> 00:26:34.610
According to our existing law, police doesn't
have any right to take into custody anyone

00:26:34.610 --> 00:26:38.419
for the sake of protecting even demonstrators.

00:26:38.419 --> 00:26:47.370
While in�for example, in France, twenty-four
hours police can take, forty-eight hours prosecutor

00:26:47.370 --> 00:26:51.769
can keep him just for investigation.

00:26:51.769 --> 00:26:55.470
In Britain it is thirty-six hours for police.

00:26:55.470 --> 00:26:58.269
In Turkey police doesn't have such a right.

00:26:58.269 --> 00:27:09.039
Now with this new law we are giving the same
standard of French rule�law.

00:27:09.039 --> 00:27:11.629
And we give the right in extraordinary situation.

00:27:11.629 --> 00:27:21.049
In certain cases when there is a violent�violence
in any action, police can take for twenty-four

00:27:21.049 --> 00:27:24.440
hours to custody and prosecutor for forty-eight
hours.

00:27:24.440 --> 00:27:27.389
This is the minimum in EU standards.

00:27:27.389 --> 00:27:32.289
In all other EU countries, that is much higher.

00:27:32.289 --> 00:27:38.429
In some countries like Spain I think forty-eight
hours and thirty-six to seventy-two hours

00:27:38.429 --> 00:27:40.070
in some countries.

00:27:40.070 --> 00:27:46.799
So there is not any single article or item
which is contradictory with European standards.

00:27:46.799 --> 00:27:50.059
HAASS: I expect there may be some more questions
on things domestic.

00:27:50.059 --> 00:27:51.629
But it is the Council on Foreign Relations.

00:27:51.629 --> 00:27:54.279
I'm going to try to get a couple of foreign
policy questions...

00:27:54.279 --> 00:27:55.279
DAVUTOGLU: Yes.

00:27:55.279 --> 00:27:56.279
HAASS: ... out there.

00:27:56.279 --> 00:28:01.710
You were famously known for saying that Turkey's
foreign policy was based on the idea with

00:28:01.710 --> 00:28:05.889
no problems with any of your neighbors.

00:28:05.889 --> 00:28:08.769
But now you're at war with the government
of Syria.

00:28:08.769 --> 00:28:13.649
And you're estranged, I would say, from both
Egypt and Israel.

00:28:13.649 --> 00:28:16.299
What's gone wrong?

00:28:16.299 --> 00:28:18.080
DAVUTOGLU: Yes.

00:28:18.080 --> 00:28:20.340
We declared zero problems with our neighbors.

00:28:20.340 --> 00:28:26.429
The important thing is whether you have a
counterpart in your neighbor or not.

00:28:26.429 --> 00:28:34.440
When�for example, regarding Syria, when
there was a counterpart, when Bashar Assad

00:28:34.440 --> 00:28:40.580
was not killing his people, we are not intervening
in their domestic affairs.

00:28:40.580 --> 00:28:48.160
But when Bashar Assad started to kill his
people and refugees came to Turkey, and when

00:28:48.160 --> 00:28:49.160
he...

00:28:49.160 --> 00:28:50.160
HAASS: How many refugees are now in Turkey?

00:28:50.160 --> 00:28:53.350
DAVUTOGLU: Two million refugees from Syria
and Iraq.

00:28:53.350 --> 00:28:54.610
You can imagine.

00:28:54.610 --> 00:28:58.649
Almost 10 percent of Syrians now are living
in Turkey.

00:28:58.649 --> 00:29:06.240
And in some Turkish towns like Kilis the number
of Syrians are more than the number of Turks.

00:29:06.240 --> 00:29:10.929
And in this condition problem is in Syria.

00:29:10.929 --> 00:29:17.639
And you don't have someone in Damascus you
are able to talk.

00:29:17.639 --> 00:29:22.640
Because despite of all of our efforts, to
convince him not to use his army against the

00:29:22.640 --> 00:29:25.159
people, he used chemical weapons.

00:29:25.159 --> 00:29:29.059
He used Scud missiles against civilians.

00:29:29.059 --> 00:29:33.480
You have problem if you don't have problems
with such a person.

00:29:33.480 --> 00:29:38.590
You have problem with your values if you don't
have problem with such a person.

00:29:38.590 --> 00:29:44.720
So it is�it was not our fault because of
this bad relation with Syria.

00:29:44.720 --> 00:29:48.220
But values, there is always priority of the
values.

00:29:48.220 --> 00:29:54.330
The most important value in politics and social
life is human dignity.

00:29:54.330 --> 00:29:59.960
Having zero problems with neighbors is secondary
compared to this basic principle.

00:29:59.960 --> 00:30:04.639
It's right, yes, we had good relations.

00:30:04.639 --> 00:30:10.710
And I was mediator between Israel and Syria
when Bashar Assad was not killing his people.

00:30:10.710 --> 00:30:15.940
When Israeli armies were not attacking to
Gaza, children of Gaza, we had good relations.

00:30:15.940 --> 00:30:23.590
And in 2008 December we were very close to
final settlement between Israel and Syria.

00:30:23.590 --> 00:30:30.110
December 8, I still remember the date, Israeli
Prime Minister Ehud Olmert stayed in residence

00:30:30.110 --> 00:30:34.440
of prime minister then Erdogan in a room.

00:30:34.440 --> 00:30:41.260
In the other room we were talking with Bashar
Assad by phone to finalize the deal.

00:30:41.260 --> 00:30:43.559
Telephone mediation let me say.

00:30:43.559 --> 00:30:51.650
And in one week we were supposed to have a
summit, Turkey, Israel, Syria to finalize

00:30:51.650 --> 00:30:52.650
the deal.

00:30:52.650 --> 00:30:54.830
And all the paper were ready except one word.

00:30:54.830 --> 00:30:58.279
And I was given the task to complete this
in three days.

00:30:58.279 --> 00:31:05.820
When we completed this Friday evening, Saturday
morning Israeli army attack Gaza and hundreds

00:31:05.820 --> 00:31:07.840
of Gazan people were killed.

00:31:07.840 --> 00:31:09.510
So it was not our choice.

00:31:09.510 --> 00:31:15.320
We did everything to have good relations with
Israel, with Syria.

00:31:15.320 --> 00:31:18.700
But it was not our choice.

00:31:18.700 --> 00:31:21.640
Except that today we have excellent relations
with Greece.

00:31:21.640 --> 00:31:26.100
(Inaudible) legislature cooperation (inaudible)
mechanism with Bulgaria.

00:31:26.100 --> 00:31:32.350
We're with Iran balanced and we don't have
any direct problem with them.

00:31:32.350 --> 00:31:34.429
With Iraq now we have excellent relations.

00:31:34.429 --> 00:31:38.100
We had problem with Maliki because of his
sectarian policy.

00:31:38.100 --> 00:31:41.750
But one of the visit if Prime Minister Abadi
was to Turkey.

00:31:41.750 --> 00:31:43.940
I went to Baghdad.

00:31:43.940 --> 00:31:46.340
And we have good relations with Russia.

00:31:46.340 --> 00:31:50.309
We have high level cooperation with Ukraine.

00:31:50.309 --> 00:31:53.820
Interestingly with Russia and Ukraine, we
are keeping the same level of good relations.

00:31:53.820 --> 00:31:57.540
With Azerbaijan, with Georgia we don't have
even ID.

00:31:57.540 --> 00:32:00.750
We don't need passport to go to Georgia and
come.

00:32:00.750 --> 00:32:04.750
So our policy's still there.

00:32:04.750 --> 00:32:08.909
But whether we have proper counterpart to
implement this policy, it is not our choice.

00:32:08.909 --> 00:32:11.960
It is the�it is given to us unfortunately.

00:32:11.960 --> 00:32:15.240
HAASS: In the list you gave, then fact that
you don't have a problem in your relations

00:32:15.240 --> 00:32:16.769
with Russia is a problem.

00:32:16.769 --> 00:32:18.049
DAVUTOGLU: No.

00:32:18.049 --> 00:32:22.429
(LAUGHTER)
HAASS: But Turkey is�the view here is that

00:32:22.429 --> 00:32:28.070
Turkey is so dependent on Russia for Turkey's
imports of natural gas, 60 or whatever percent,

00:32:28.070 --> 00:32:33.220
that Turkey has been unwilling to isolate
Russia for what it has done in Ukraine.

00:32:33.220 --> 00:32:35.320
DAVUTOGLU: Not only Ukraine.

00:32:35.320 --> 00:32:40.590
Let me ask why didn't we isolate Russia because
of supporting Assad regime?

00:32:40.590 --> 00:32:50.630
Why U.S. and others didn't isolate Russia
when Russia supported Assad who killed 300,000

00:32:50.630 --> 00:32:51.630
people?

00:32:51.630 --> 00:32:56.850
Is it because of�that those people who were
killed were Muslims and Syrians, and those

00:32:56.850 --> 00:32:59.870
who were killed in Ukraine were Christians
and Ukrainian?

00:32:59.870 --> 00:33:01.620
Is that the difference?

00:33:01.620 --> 00:33:05.749
If Russia did wrong, we have to be consistent.

00:33:05.749 --> 00:33:09.110
They did wrong in Syria.

00:33:09.110 --> 00:33:10.389
What was the response?

00:33:10.389 --> 00:33:13.999
What was the response?

00:33:13.999 --> 00:33:17.809
And I am not blaming on one person or two.

00:33:17.809 --> 00:33:23.950
But there were very high level contacts between
European and American allies with Russia when

00:33:23.950 --> 00:33:32.019
Russians were supporting Bashar Assad to kill
hundreds of thousands of people, and to force

00:33:32.019 --> 00:33:34.049
millions of them to Turkey.

00:33:34.049 --> 00:33:41.249
We have been telling that we have to be firm
in U.N. to protect civilians in Syria.

00:33:41.249 --> 00:33:42.740
But in Ukraine as well.

00:33:42.740 --> 00:33:44.139
Our position is very clear.

00:33:44.139 --> 00:33:49.149
And Putin�President Putin, when he came
to Ankara, we have spoken with him in a very

00:33:49.149 --> 00:33:50.149
clear manner.

00:33:50.149 --> 00:33:52.749
HAASS: But you have not supported sanctions
against Russia...

00:33:52.749 --> 00:33:53.749
DAVUTOGLU: No.

00:33:53.749 --> 00:33:54.749
I will tell you.

00:33:54.749 --> 00:33:55.749
I will come to that point.

00:33:55.749 --> 00:33:57.480
Our mind was very clear.

00:33:57.480 --> 00:34:00.999
We told him that Turkish position is clear.

00:34:00.999 --> 00:34:07.289
We will never, never compromise from territorial
integrity of Ukraine.

00:34:07.289 --> 00:34:13.350
And we expect respect to Crimean Tatars in
Crimea.

00:34:13.350 --> 00:34:16.800
And we don't want any tension in Black Sea.

00:34:16.800 --> 00:34:21.030
So this is our national position.

00:34:21.030 --> 00:34:26.899
But we are not acting in a vacuum, as I said.

00:34:26.899 --> 00:34:37.690
And we have certain critical cooperation with
Russia, on energy for example, and others.

00:34:37.690 --> 00:34:40.429
Our Ukrainian friends understand very well.

00:34:40.429 --> 00:34:51.329
And today a Turkish diplomat is in charge
of OSCE efforts and special envoy in Ukraine,

00:34:51.329 --> 00:34:57.790
and brought Ukrainian and Russian side, respect
Turkish policy and prefer a Turkish diplomat

00:34:57.790 --> 00:35:00.240
to run this type of mediation effort.

00:35:00.240 --> 00:35:03.130
We will keep our principal position.

00:35:03.130 --> 00:35:07.450
Turkish foreign policy is a foreign policy
of principle.

00:35:07.450 --> 00:35:10.819
We don't say we support democracy in New York.

00:35:10.819 --> 00:35:13.349
We support democracy in Cairo.

00:35:13.349 --> 00:35:15.890
We support democracy in Damascus.

00:35:15.890 --> 00:35:19.310
It is easy to preach democracy in Western
capitals.

00:35:19.310 --> 00:35:26.430
It is difficult to say the truth when there
was a military coup in Egypt.

00:35:26.430 --> 00:35:31.320
And this even taking risk to lose Turkish
interest.

00:35:31.320 --> 00:35:33.060
It was difficult.

00:35:33.060 --> 00:35:35.809
But our position was very clear there as well.

00:35:35.809 --> 00:35:37.750
We respect Egyptian culture.

00:35:37.750 --> 00:35:39.160
We respect Egyptian history.

00:35:39.160 --> 00:35:41.049
We respect Egyptian civilization.

00:35:41.049 --> 00:35:47.540
And today I said in a meeting that Egypt is
the backbone, strategic backbone of peace

00:35:47.540 --> 00:35:49.420
and stability in the region.

00:35:49.420 --> 00:36:00.150
But for so many years when democracy was advised
to other societies, it was a test for all

00:36:00.150 --> 00:36:01.150
of us.

00:36:01.150 --> 00:36:06.750
Similarly, now in Ukraine, there should be
a democratic process.

00:36:06.750 --> 00:36:12.880
Ukraine is our strategic partner and Russia
is our�Turkey's the only country neighbor

00:36:12.880 --> 00:36:17.049
who brought Ukraine and Russia and having
access to Crimea.

00:36:17.049 --> 00:36:23.819
We cannot risk everything based on certain
processes which we didn't initiate, which

00:36:23.819 --> 00:36:28.349
we were not consulted.

00:36:28.349 --> 00:36:32.869
In EU, I raised as minister of foreign affairs
about Ukrainian issue.

00:36:32.869 --> 00:36:34.620
We support Ukraine.

00:36:34.620 --> 00:36:38.080
We will defend the right to territory integrity
of Ukraine.

00:36:38.080 --> 00:36:40.109
But nobody consulted us.

00:36:40.109 --> 00:36:45.260
Although we were neighbor to Ukraine, nobody
consulted us about what will be happening

00:36:45.260 --> 00:36:46.480
in Ukraine.

00:36:46.480 --> 00:36:52.099
When�this is of course another criticism
I am raising.

00:36:52.099 --> 00:36:57.890
After a while if you do not prevent a crisis
at early stage, you have to be ready for a

00:36:57.890 --> 00:37:01.099
much bigger problem in the future.

00:37:01.099 --> 00:37:06.640
Unfortunately, we were not�when I say we
I mean our allies in NATO, Trans-Atlantic

00:37:06.640 --> 00:37:07.640
Alliance.

00:37:07.640 --> 00:37:11.960
We were not very efficient to prevent a crisis
at early stage.

00:37:11.960 --> 00:37:15.240
In 2008 Georgian crisis.

00:37:15.240 --> 00:37:19.270
It was easy to say something from outside.

00:37:19.270 --> 00:37:22.069
But Georgia is our neighbor.

00:37:22.069 --> 00:37:28.050
When the crisis in Georgia emerged, Prime
Minister Erdogan and all of us, we went immediately

00:37:28.050 --> 00:37:32.960
to Georgia to visit, and to Moscow in order
to ease the tension.

00:37:32.960 --> 00:37:40.230
As a growing economy and as a stable democracy,
Turkey doesn't want to see any instability

00:37:40.230 --> 00:37:41.330
around itself.

00:37:41.330 --> 00:37:45.920
We want to see stability and easing the tension.

00:37:45.920 --> 00:37:50.040
That is mainly why we are approaching to Ukraine
in this framework.

00:37:50.040 --> 00:37:56.210
HAASS: I will show uncharacteristic self-restraint
and just raise two other questions.

00:37:56.210 --> 00:38:00.410
One deals with�one with the Middle East,
one with Europe.

00:38:00.410 --> 00:38:03.130
I'll do the European one.

00:38:03.130 --> 00:38:06.890
Do you think in your career you will ever
see Turkey in the EU?

00:38:06.890 --> 00:38:09.309
DAVUTOGLU: Yes.

00:38:09.309 --> 00:38:11.740
It depends.

00:38:11.740 --> 00:38:16.050
It depends of course the will of two sides.

00:38:16.050 --> 00:38:20.890
We�if you ask me do you want to see Turkey
in EU, yes.

00:38:20.890 --> 00:38:29.950
But if you ask do you think that will happen,
I cannot judge on behalf of Europeans who

00:38:29.950 --> 00:38:33.260
have so many excuses not to accept Turkey.

00:38:33.260 --> 00:38:38.960
It was interesting in 2002 I was chief adviser
to Prime Minister Erdogan when we participated

00:38:38.960 --> 00:38:40.809
first EU summit.

00:38:40.809 --> 00:38:51.299
And then as chief I had�I negotiated with
leading European teams about our procedure.

00:38:51.299 --> 00:38:54.960
At that time they were saying very frankly
sometime behind it.

00:38:54.960 --> 00:38:59.849
Saying that Turkey's too poor, too weak to
be member.

00:38:59.849 --> 00:39:05.460
Because if Turkey becomes member, European
Union has to subsidize Turkish economy.

00:39:05.460 --> 00:39:09.630
And Turks will be asking more job.

00:39:09.630 --> 00:39:17.349
Now what they are saying is Turkey's too big
and too powerful to be a member.

00:39:17.349 --> 00:39:24.190
Because of this strength it will be difficult
to absorb Turkey.

00:39:24.190 --> 00:39:28.180
If you have an intention, a good intention,
you can find a solution.

00:39:28.180 --> 00:39:31.980
But if you want to find excuses, you can find
hundreds of excuses.

00:39:31.980 --> 00:39:35.480
HAASS: Why do you think the Europeans are
looking for excuses?

00:39:35.480 --> 00:39:37.990
DAVUTOGLU: Not all Europeans.

00:39:37.990 --> 00:39:39.850
I was in Portugal before coming here.

00:39:39.850 --> 00:39:40.980
They are supporting us.

00:39:40.980 --> 00:39:42.819
In Italy they are supporting us.

00:39:42.819 --> 00:39:44.710
Poland they are supporting.

00:39:44.710 --> 00:39:46.299
Many Europeans are supporting.

00:39:46.299 --> 00:39:51.350
But for those who are reluctant, the first
is cultural prejudice.

00:39:51.350 --> 00:39:53.290
Unfortunately I have to say this.

00:39:53.290 --> 00:39:54.450
Not economic indicators.

00:39:54.450 --> 00:39:59.980
Before we were thinking that if we perform
well in economics it will be easy for Turkey

00:39:59.980 --> 00:40:02.060
skeptics in Europe to accept Turkey.

00:40:02.060 --> 00:40:07.119
But now we realize whatever we do, something�it
is difficult to change something which is

00:40:07.119 --> 00:40:08.500
cultural prejudice.

00:40:08.500 --> 00:40:14.980
As if Europe is a Christian continent, Holy
Roman Christian continent.

00:40:14.980 --> 00:40:17.910
This is not true for all Europeans.

00:40:17.910 --> 00:40:22.290
This is one cultural prejudice we have to
fight.

00:40:22.290 --> 00:40:28.289
And today Turkey's much more�and Turkish
people are much more tolerant for other cultures,

00:40:28.289 --> 00:40:37.059
and much more ready to be inclusive and to
be in Europe than (inaudible) moment in Germany.

00:40:37.059 --> 00:40:44.849
Or some xenophobic and Islamophobic type of
tendencies in Europe.

00:40:44.849 --> 00:40:54.220
Second is a fear of a rising Turkey because
Turkish economy, Turkish population is dynamic.

00:40:54.220 --> 00:40:58.630
History doesn't forgive wrong decisions in
wrong time.

00:40:58.630 --> 00:41:05.119
And history doesn't forget stagnation or being
static.

00:41:05.119 --> 00:41:09.470
If an empire�it happened to Ottoman Empire,
it happened to Roman Empire, it happened to

00:41:09.470 --> 00:41:15.559
all imperial tradition in the bag (ph), and
all big traditions�if they start to think

00:41:15.559 --> 00:41:22.690
statically, in a static way, not to receive
others, then you�that state or civilization

00:41:22.690 --> 00:41:24.049
start to decline.

00:41:24.049 --> 00:41:31.390
The most historic turning point of Roman Empire
was the era of Marcus Aurelius, who tried

00:41:31.390 --> 00:41:33.599
to transform Roman society.

00:41:33.599 --> 00:41:38.549
But when it was not possible to be more inclusive
based on straight philosophy.

00:41:38.549 --> 00:41:43.660
But when it was not successful, Roman Empire
started to decline.

00:41:43.660 --> 00:41:47.980
Similarly now, European Union, unfortunately
they had a choice.

00:41:47.980 --> 00:41:52.059
They're at the threshold of a choice.

00:41:52.059 --> 00:42:01.141
Either they will be static in economic sense,
less influential in geopolitical sense, and

00:42:01.141 --> 00:42:06.090
less dynamic in demographic sense.

00:42:06.090 --> 00:42:13.819
They will be more inclusive in cultural sense,
more dynamic in economic sense, more relevant

00:42:13.819 --> 00:42:18.780
in world affairs in geopolitical sense.

00:42:18.780 --> 00:42:23.190
Taking Turkey into Europe is a choice between
these two Europe.

00:42:23.190 --> 00:42:26.670
If they want to have the first choice they
will not accept Turkey.

00:42:26.670 --> 00:42:32.550
If they want to have the second choice, geopolitical
relevance, dynamic and competitive economy,

00:42:32.550 --> 00:42:35.160
inclusive culture, they will accept Turkey.

00:42:35.160 --> 00:42:36.890
It is not a test for us anymore.

00:42:36.890 --> 00:42:41.830
We have�we passed our test with economic
performance, with all the criteria, democratic

00:42:41.830 --> 00:42:42.830
criteria.

00:42:42.830 --> 00:42:47.829
Now it is a test for Europeans to decide which
type of Europe they want.

00:42:47.829 --> 00:42:49.750
And we are expecting their decision.

00:42:49.750 --> 00:42:53.040
Whenever they decide, we are ready.

00:42:53.040 --> 00:42:58.480
HAASS: That seems as good a point as any to
open it up for questions from our members.

00:42:58.480 --> 00:43:00.490
It's on the record.

00:43:00.490 --> 00:43:02.000
Just wait for a microphone.

00:43:02.000 --> 00:43:06.640
Please keep your�identify yourself and keep
your question relatively succinct.

00:43:06.640 --> 00:43:09.510
I see a hand up over there, but I don't have
my glasses on.

00:43:09.510 --> 00:43:11.450
QUESTION: Thank you very much, Mr. Prime Minister.

00:43:11.450 --> 00:43:16.510
David Rivkin from Debevoise &amp; Plimpton, also
president of the International Bar Association.

00:43:16.510 --> 00:43:21.140
One of our members, the Union of Turkish Bars,
comes to very different conclusions about

00:43:21.140 --> 00:43:25.569
the internal security bill and whether it
complies with international standards.

00:43:25.569 --> 00:43:32.040
For example, not just�there's not just a
48-hour limit on police holding individuals,

00:43:32.040 --> 00:43:36.530
but governors and other administrative officials
may hold people.

00:43:36.530 --> 00:43:41.250
The ban on covering one's face would apply
even in the event that the police sprayed

00:43:41.250 --> 00:43:44.299
the protestors with pepper spray.

00:43:44.299 --> 00:43:48.790
And they have other criticisms of it so that
it does not meet EUstandards.

00:43:48.790 --> 00:43:53.260
But in addition they have pointed out that
the government is taking steps to bring control

00:43:53.260 --> 00:43:57.500
of lawyers, regulation of lawyers under the
judiciary, which the government controls,

00:43:57.500 --> 00:44:02.280
rather than maintaining them as an independent
profession, which is very important in preserving

00:44:02.280 --> 00:44:03.700
democracy.

00:44:03.700 --> 00:44:07.960
Why is the government taking steps to control
the regulation of lawyers?

00:44:07.960 --> 00:44:13.650
DAVUTOGLU: First of all, I know all the text
of the law.

00:44:13.650 --> 00:44:16.430
And we discussed in the cabinet hours and
hours.

00:44:16.430 --> 00:44:23.430
You know what they mean by these�giving
the right of decision to governors.

00:44:23.430 --> 00:44:27.740
Not governors, not higher authority.

00:44:27.740 --> 00:44:34.320
Instead of giving this authority to police,
because police is a man with gun.

00:44:34.320 --> 00:44:36.150
And he might be nervous.

00:44:36.150 --> 00:44:40.380
He might be in a situation which he can't
decide on its own.

00:44:40.380 --> 00:44:45.610
The�those�the decision will be taken by
prosecutor.

00:44:45.610 --> 00:44:54.619
But if it is urgent like what happened in
6 and 7 October, four young men were killed

00:44:54.619 --> 00:45:00.280
in front of police, pushed�were thrown from
the building.

00:45:00.280 --> 00:45:05.430
And police were�legally were not able to
control the situation.

00:45:05.430 --> 00:45:12.940
What we are saying is that not police, but
a higher civilian authority will decide temporarily

00:45:12.940 --> 00:45:18.880
until prosecutor comes or takes the decision.

00:45:18.880 --> 00:45:24.829
They can take the decision just for twenty-four
hours.

00:45:24.829 --> 00:45:29.300
If you give this to police it will be much
more difficult to control.

00:45:29.300 --> 00:45:36.950
And you and I, we all of us we know how the
rules are in the United States.

00:45:36.950 --> 00:45:39.460
Assume that you are driving a car.

00:45:39.460 --> 00:45:41.280
You are driving a car.

00:45:41.280 --> 00:45:45.150
If a police here in New York stops you, you
stop.

00:45:45.150 --> 00:45:47.170
And he can check.

00:45:47.170 --> 00:45:50.559
And it is�you have to keep your hand.

00:45:50.559 --> 00:45:51.799
You cannot move your hand.

00:45:51.799 --> 00:45:53.089
Is that right?

00:45:53.089 --> 00:46:03.970
In Turkey a police, even if there is an intelligence
report that a car is carrying a gun or bonsai

00:46:03.970 --> 00:46:14.280
(ph) type of materials, a police cannot stop
and check.

00:46:14.280 --> 00:46:18.240
He has to take decision from the court.

00:46:18.240 --> 00:46:24.670
And court says bring me the evidence, then
I will give you permission.

00:46:24.670 --> 00:46:30.940
We have realized that because of this it was
impossible to prevent�to act proactively

00:46:30.940 --> 00:46:33.119
to prevent crime.

00:46:33.119 --> 00:46:40.880
In Europe and United States and everywhere,
police has the right to check if there is

00:46:40.880 --> 00:46:47.039
a clear�if there is information that there
is something in the car.

00:46:47.039 --> 00:46:49.750
In existing Turkish law, we don't have this.

00:46:49.750 --> 00:46:55.319
And our party brought this law in 2004 and
2005 with good intention.

00:46:55.319 --> 00:47:00.510
But now after so many experiences we realized
that it is better to adapt American and European

00:47:00.510 --> 00:47:01.770
standards.

00:47:01.770 --> 00:47:07.760
And Turkey's not much more safe and secure
than these countries when you have so many

00:47:07.760 --> 00:47:16.220
ISIS militants, maybe agents of Syrian regime,
and terrorists from different groups.

00:47:16.220 --> 00:47:18.510
We have taken this caution.

00:47:18.510 --> 00:47:26.109
I can give you�send you, please�our embassy
can send you all this information one-by-one

00:47:26.109 --> 00:47:27.319
about justification.

00:47:27.319 --> 00:47:35.599
About lawyers, I mean the high board of prosecutors
and judges.

00:47:35.599 --> 00:47:47.490
You know before us, before 2010 referendum,
constitution referendum, this court was elected

00:47:47.490 --> 00:47:50.279
within a group, very limited group.

00:47:50.279 --> 00:47:54.670
What we did, our government did this in 2010.

00:47:54.670 --> 00:48:03.310
We said that since judges and prosecutors
are the most respected people, they have to

00:48:03.310 --> 00:48:07.369
choose their own high board, not government.

00:48:07.369 --> 00:48:10.510
Not just a small circle.

00:48:10.510 --> 00:48:19.809
And based on that, today in this high court
there is a high board of prosecutors and judges.

00:48:19.809 --> 00:48:21.500
They are voting.

00:48:21.500 --> 00:48:23.819
All judges and prosecutors are voting.

00:48:23.819 --> 00:48:26.940
And the body has been formed by this.

00:48:26.940 --> 00:48:34.110
We as the government, we suggested that one
man, one vote�so that nobody could come

00:48:34.110 --> 00:48:39.710
together to monopolize this high board.

00:48:39.710 --> 00:48:44.279
But unfortunately constitution court decided
that it should be a list.

00:48:44.279 --> 00:48:52.390
Once it is a list, one will dominate it, high
board, and this group had links and certain

00:48:52.390 --> 00:48:56.510
connections, networks in police and judicial
system.

00:48:56.510 --> 00:49:04.090
And many journalists, many intellectuals,
many politicians were arrested and were under

00:49:04.090 --> 00:49:10.930
risk because of this monopoly and domination
in judicial system, this parallel structure

00:49:10.930 --> 00:49:13.190
what you call.

00:49:13.190 --> 00:49:18.230
Now there is�we didn't change the rule.

00:49:18.230 --> 00:49:27.400
There has been another election and a group
of different ideologies, Sudanese, Alawites,

00:49:27.400 --> 00:49:33.880
different sects, groups, leftist, rightist,
they formed another list.

00:49:33.880 --> 00:49:36.070
And now they are in the board.

00:49:36.070 --> 00:49:38.609
They are not pro-government.

00:49:38.609 --> 00:49:41.920
They are not in one group or the other group.

00:49:41.920 --> 00:49:46.779
And that body is deciding what will happen.

00:49:46.779 --> 00:49:49.800
Independence of judicial system is very important.

00:49:49.800 --> 00:49:55.680
But also not independence only from executive
power, but independence from the monopoly

00:49:55.680 --> 00:49:57.589
or domination of one group.

00:49:57.589 --> 00:50:04.510
If a seemingly religious group is dominating
the judicial system or a secular group not

00:50:04.510 --> 00:50:07.650
important, that is the end of the justice.

00:50:07.650 --> 00:50:17.730
The average judge should decide on his own
or on her own, not based on a decision taken

00:50:17.730 --> 00:50:19.940
outside the court system.

00:50:19.940 --> 00:50:22.270
That is what is happening.

00:50:22.270 --> 00:50:27.640
But if you have any suggestion or any other
question, we are ready to answer because I

00:50:27.640 --> 00:50:36.369
know, I know that there are so many speculations
and rumors circulated in United States and

00:50:36.369 --> 00:50:39.460
Europe just to blame on Turkish government.

00:50:39.460 --> 00:50:40.520
We are ready.

00:50:40.520 --> 00:50:41.530
I am challenging.

00:50:41.530 --> 00:50:43.630
We are ready to answer any question.

00:50:43.630 --> 00:50:49.549
But don't believe what some circles are just
circulating without seeing the text itself

00:50:49.549 --> 00:50:53.010
or without seeing the action itself.

00:50:53.010 --> 00:50:55.299
HAASS: We just had an invitation for more
questions.

00:50:55.299 --> 00:50:59.420
So anything about domestic, foreign policy
or economic policy.

00:50:59.420 --> 00:51:01.670
I saw a hand there.

00:51:01.670 --> 00:51:02.670
Yes, sir?

00:51:02.670 --> 00:51:05.190
QUESTION: Phil Waldeck from Prudential Financial.

00:51:05.190 --> 00:51:10.510
I'd be interested in the Prime Minister's
thoughts on Turkey's policies to combat the

00:51:10.510 --> 00:51:11.510
threat of ISIS.

00:51:11.510 --> 00:51:17.430
And under what circumstances Turkey would
consider using ground troops to combat ISIS.

00:51:17.430 --> 00:51:23.069
HAASS: Also in you answer to that also add
a little bit about what more you could do

00:51:23.069 --> 00:51:29.590
to stop the flow of recruits from around the
world transiting Turkey to beef up ISIS.

00:51:29.590 --> 00:51:34.150
DAVUTOGLU: First of all, let us clarify this
group ISIS.

00:51:34.150 --> 00:51:36.010
How did they emerge?

00:51:36.010 --> 00:51:43.720
ISIS did come to the picture of Syrian scene
in 2013, March.

00:51:43.720 --> 00:51:48.119
Means after two years of Syrian crisis.

00:51:48.119 --> 00:51:56.029
And in that two years around 200,000 people
were killed, so�and millions were already

00:51:56.029 --> 00:51:57.549
refugees.

00:51:57.549 --> 00:52:03.200
So there is now�we are very short memory
we have.

00:52:03.200 --> 00:52:07.000
There is an impression now as if Syrian crisis
is ISIL crisis.

00:52:07.000 --> 00:52:09.440
If you eliminate ISIL, there will be no Syrian
crisis.

00:52:09.440 --> 00:52:10.960
It's not true.

00:52:10.960 --> 00:52:15.289
ISIL did emerge after two years of Syrian
crisis.

00:52:15.289 --> 00:52:21.680
Even if you eliminate ISIL today�which we
have to do�we have to fight and we have

00:52:21.680 --> 00:52:22.680
to eliminate.

00:52:22.680 --> 00:52:31.860
Another radical group may emerge, not ISIL,
but PISIL or IKIL (ph), whatever it is.

00:52:31.860 --> 00:52:34.250
Based on the same�in the same context.

00:52:34.250 --> 00:52:36.150
Where did they come from?

00:52:36.150 --> 00:52:37.940
Not from Turkey.

00:52:37.940 --> 00:52:42.900
Some people are propagating this as if there's
a transit to ISIL from Turkey.

00:52:42.900 --> 00:52:44.059
No.

00:52:44.059 --> 00:52:54.480
ISIL before was Iraqi Islamic State, IIL,
which was formed in 2003 by another Baghdadi

00:52:54.480 --> 00:52:56.090
linked to Al-Qaeda.

00:52:56.090 --> 00:53:04.079
And this Baghdadi, the terrorist, leader of
this terrorist group, was in Abu Ghraib prison

00:53:04.079 --> 00:53:07.270
under the control of�when U.S. forces are
there.

00:53:07.270 --> 00:53:14.240
And stayed there after�until after the withdrawal
of American troops.

00:53:14.240 --> 00:53:19.960
And they came from Iraqi territories to Syria.

00:53:19.960 --> 00:53:23.200
They entered Syria from Iraq.

00:53:23.200 --> 00:53:29.859
And when they entered, Syrian regime didn't
do anything against them.

00:53:29.859 --> 00:53:34.400
In fact, some of them were released from Syrian
prisons.

00:53:34.400 --> 00:53:36.309
Because we have intelligence experience.

00:53:36.309 --> 00:53:45.640
I was mediating between Iraq and Syria in
2009 when Maliki accused Bashar Assad to organize

00:53:45.640 --> 00:53:49.750
terrorist attacks in Baghdad.

00:53:49.750 --> 00:53:51.920
Syrian regime had contacts with this group.

00:53:51.920 --> 00:54:01.230
From 2013 March until 2014 June, until they
attacked Mosul there was no single clash between

00:54:01.230 --> 00:54:03.640
the Syrian regime and ISIL.

00:54:03.640 --> 00:54:08.420
ISIL controlled Deir ez-Zor, which was under
the control of Free Syrian Army.

00:54:08.420 --> 00:54:14.329
Then took over Raqqah, which was under the
control of Free Syrian Army, moderated position.

00:54:14.329 --> 00:54:17.319
Then Manbij, then Jarabulus.

00:54:17.319 --> 00:54:18.750
How did they control?

00:54:18.750 --> 00:54:24.320
Because Syrian air strikes, air forces bombarded
these places.

00:54:24.320 --> 00:54:32.180
And not only Syrian forces, Free Syrian Army
head to evacuate and ISIL came in.

00:54:32.180 --> 00:54:37.940
So there was a tactical coalition between
regime and ISIL.

00:54:37.940 --> 00:54:44.490
When did this change when they attack back
to Mosul?

00:54:44.490 --> 00:54:50.539
Until that time, ISIL was not in the agenda
of Iraqi or Syrian regime.

00:54:50.539 --> 00:54:51.690
Syrian regime especially.

00:54:51.690 --> 00:54:53.630
Now there is such a threat.

00:54:53.630 --> 00:54:54.880
What should be done?

00:54:54.880 --> 00:54:58.359
We have to do everything to prevent them.

00:54:58.359 --> 00:55:04.069
There is no other country more threatened
than Turkey because of this ISIL.

00:55:04.069 --> 00:55:10.869
Because we have 1,295 kilometer long Iraq
and Syria border.

00:55:10.869 --> 00:55:15.010
And 60 percent of this border is under ISIL
control.

00:55:15.010 --> 00:55:17.940
We cannot tolerate this.

00:55:17.940 --> 00:55:19.790
But what is the method?

00:55:19.790 --> 00:55:22.450
How will we do it?

00:55:22.450 --> 00:55:30.609
The method is we have to have a grand, integrated
strategy for Syria and for Iraq, but especially

00:55:30.609 --> 00:55:31.609
for Syria.

00:55:31.609 --> 00:55:36.460
In Syria the job is more difficult for us
because there is no counterpart in Damascus.

00:55:36.460 --> 00:55:39.119
In Baghdad at least we have a counterpart.

00:55:39.119 --> 00:55:40.790
We can work together.

00:55:40.790 --> 00:55:45.410
Our minister of defense is�was in Baghdad
yesterday, and today in Erbil.

00:55:45.410 --> 00:55:51.369
And we send two full of equipment to airplane
to Baghdad.

00:55:51.369 --> 00:55:57.289
And we are training Peshmerga, Turkish forces
are training Peshmerga and also Mosul people

00:55:57.289 --> 00:56:00.970
in order to liberate Mosul.

00:56:00.970 --> 00:56:03.880
But in Syria with who will we work?

00:56:03.880 --> 00:56:05.610
This is the question.

00:56:05.610 --> 00:56:09.579
We have been asking this question, and for
last four years we have been telling too American

00:56:09.579 --> 00:56:15.619
friends, European friends that moderate forces
should be supported.

00:56:15.619 --> 00:56:19.039
There was no support to moderate forces.

00:56:19.039 --> 00:56:21.930
Because of this power vacuum they took over
the control.

00:56:21.930 --> 00:56:27.240
When did they become a real threat as an army,
as if they're army, this ISIL?

00:56:27.240 --> 00:56:34.569
When they took over sophisticated American
weapons in Mosul which were left by Iraqi

00:56:34.569 --> 00:56:44.490
army, bag (ph), tanks, armed vehicles, heavy
weapons of Iraqi army were taken by ISIL.

00:56:44.490 --> 00:56:50.549
Until that time ISIL was the balance of power
between Free Syrian Army and ISIL was almost

00:56:50.549 --> 00:56:54.619
equal because of light weapons.

00:56:54.619 --> 00:56:58.040
But ISIL took these weapons.

00:56:58.040 --> 00:56:59.820
Many of them are American weapons.

00:56:59.820 --> 00:57:04.490
Of course I don't blame United States because
they gave this to Iraqi army and Iraqi army

00:57:04.490 --> 00:57:05.490
left them.

